# Governance

Nexy is an open-source project governed by its maintainers. This document describes how decisions are made and how the project is managed.

## Core principles

- **Community first** — changes must benefit the broader ecosystem
- **Backward compatibility** — breaking changes require deprecation warnings and migration guides
- **Minimal standard library** — prefer composable primitives over monolithic features
- **Performance matters** — every feature must justify its cost in startup time, build time, and runtime overhead

## Decision-making

### Day-to-day decisions

Routine changes (bug fixes, small features, documentation) follow the standard PR process:

1. Submit a PR
2. At least one maintainer reviews
3. All quality gates pass (lint, format, typecheck, tests)
4. Maintainer merges via squash-merge

### Significant changes

Major features, breaking changes, and architecture decisions go through an RFC (Request for Comments) process:

1. **Proposal** — open a GitHub Discussion with the RFC template
2. **Discussion** — community and maintainers provide feedback (minimum 1 week)
3. **Refinement** — proposal author addresses feedback
4. **Decision** — maintainers reach consensus and vote if needed
5. **Implementation** — RFC is accepted and implemented via PR

### Voting

When consensus cannot be reached, maintainers vote:

- Simple majority for most decisions
- Supermajority (2/3) for changes to governance or core principles
- The project lead has veto power on architecture decisions

## Maintainer roles

### Core maintainers

Full commit access and responsibility for the project. Core maintainers:

- Review and merge PRs
- Triage and label issues
- Manage releases and versioning
- Set project direction

### Becoming a maintainer

Contributors who demonstrate sustained, high-quality contributions may be invited to become maintainers. There is no fixed timeline — it depends on the depth and consistency of contributions.

## Release process

Nexy follows [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/):

- **Patch** — bug fixes and minor improvements (no breaking changes)
- **Minor** — new features, deprecations (no breaking changes)
- **Major** — breaking changes (always preceded by deprecation warnings)

Releases are cut by maintainers following the [release workflow](/community/contributor#release-process-maintainers-only).

## Code of conduct

All participants in the Nexy community are expected to follow the [Code of Conduct](https://github.com/NexyPy/nexy/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md). Violations should be reported to the maintainers.
